<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="473b022f">&lt;p&gt;
    Ensure training logistics sync with project milestones and take into account when skills are needed during
    implementation.&amp;nbsp; Decreasing the gap between knowledge acquistion and knowledge usage (on the job)&amp;nbsp; correlates
    with increases in training effectiveness.&amp;nbsp; Part of the process of developing the schedule includes finalizing
    trainers, communicating training sessions and updating collateral around learner needs (as curriculum development often
    uncovers new learner needs).
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop initial training schedule for all courses and locations that captures how how training will be rolled out
        such as by end user, role, team, or location.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work with the key stakeholders to understand any constraints around the schedule such as non-working days, shift
        patterns, or black out periods.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Share the initial training schedule with other program team to test and highlight dependencies, agree with key
        stakeholders, and engage any active business readiness networks
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
</reference>
